matrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}11 \\\\ -15 \\\\ 25 \\\\ 16\\end{bmatrix}-5\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ l\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 15 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that \n$l=3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319047 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "33586620-e110-5a37-874f-a92103c5e9fb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for One Coefficient in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ef7a933-e25a-53f9-8029-20032af40044" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317617} {:answer/id #uuid "9b77d5ab-caa5-55ab-a2eb-19df2a01588b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318096} {:answer/id #uuid "a345a44b-c232-5f9b-95d9-d833914ac12c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318125} {:answer/id #uuid "a5f4c69f-a3d2-5b2e-a4f1-2cbf710d3530" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318136} {:answer/id #uuid "db5fd3b6-f534-51c2-8e4a-d49452bf7c7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318299}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b77d5ab-caa5-55ab-a2eb-19df2a01588b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318096} :answer-field/id #uuid "18122832-a71e-5571-885b-b5abdf5b4fd3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318478}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3695980d-a1ca-52c3-a275-096dc38f4d3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-34602" :question/problem "Find $k$, if $8{a}_{1}+k{a}_{2}=0$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $k$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{a}_{1}+k{a}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 8\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}+k\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ k\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}-8\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ k\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}24 \\\\ -48 \\\\ 32\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the first components, we get \n\n$$\n-2k=24\\,⟹\\,k=-12.\n$$\n\nBut then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-12\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}24 \\\\ -36 \\\\ 48\\end{bmatrix}\\ne \\begin{bmatrix}24 \\\\ -48 \\\\ 32\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there is no $k$ such that \n $8{a}_{1}+k{a}_{2}=0.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419107 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "33586620-e110-5a37-874f-a92103c5e9fb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for One Coefficient in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1715fd90-ec78-5246-a305-0bc79c6d6201" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419101} {:answer/id #uuid "6737f66e-5883-51c4-b5ee-f853d82f7a52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419102} {:answer/id #uuid "9beb45ed-f52f-5f55-aced-c84e6915532b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419103} {:answer/id #uuid "b56988f7-12ae-5627-bee9-3cfcc596e9cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419104} {:answer/id #uuid "ceaa277a-f8cc-5c5e-8f5b-4a33f9